Source: libtiffanydb
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Maintainer: Tiffany DB Maintainers <tiffanydb@example.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               libc6-dev
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libtiffanydb1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Tiffany DB runtime library (shared object, ABI 1)
 Tiffany DB is an embedded SQL engine written in C. This package ships the
 shared object that consumers link against at run time: it opens a database,
 executes SQL and returns rows.
 .
 This is the run-time half. It contains only the shared object and the SONAME
 symlink. Headers, the static library and the pkg-config metadata are in
 libtiffanydb-dev.
 .
 The object pins roughly 3 MiB of .bss, so a process that loads it grows by
 about that much in resident memory regardless of how small the file is.

Package: libtiffanydb-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
# Sem ${shlibs:Depends}: este pacote nao contem nenhuma biblioteca partilhada
# real, so o arquivo estatico e o symlink de link. Quem liga contra a .a
# resolve os simbolos com o seu proprio linker, e a dependencia de execucao e
# da libtiffanydb1, declarada logo a seguir.
Depends: libtiffanydb1 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Tiffany DB development files (headers, static library, pkg-config)
 Headers, the static library, the linker symlink and the pkg-config file
 needed to build programs against Tiffany DB.
 .
 The installed public headers are sql_api.h and pgwire_api.h. They declare
 exactly the 39 symbols the shared object exports, and no others. Internal
 headers are not installed.
 .
 pkg-config reports version 1.0.0.